                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>Telegram 112 to Addis Ababa, October 14, 1953, informed the Embassy that the
                    President had approved a recommendation that Emperor Haile Selassie be invited
                    to visit the United States in 1954 and suggested April or May for the visit.
                    Addis Ababa telegram 148, October 19, reported that the Ambassador had
                    personally extended the President’s invitation to the Emperor. Documentation is
                    in Department of State file 775.11.</p>
            </div>
